169 0 obj
<</AP<</N 400 0 R >>/DA(/ArialNarrow 10 Tf 0 g)/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/MK<<>>/P 138 0 R /Rect[ 63.0998 283.40399 577.54102 370.92999]/Subtype/Widget/T(Text16)/Type/Annot/V(OSBA's primary objective is to support School Board Directors. That support shows itself in providing ongoing training options; governance support around policy implementation; expanded lobbying partnerships in State & Federal legislation; overall leadership education. These areas focus on improving education outcomes for the students in the state of Oregon. )>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<</AP<</N 403 0 R >>/DA(/ArialNarrow 10 Tf 0 g)/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/MK<<>>/P 138 0 R /Rect[ 63.504299 185.51801 577.54102 270.61801]/Subtype/Widget/T(Text17)/Type/Annot/V(Education is in constant flux. The methods change, the content changes, and the necessary outcomes change.  We build on past success, and look to the next challenge. We support our community, and are the conduit for accurate information about student education. OSBA gives board members the tools to succeed; that means focusing on the student needs, and having timely and accurate info . We support each other, so everyone can succeed. )>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<</AP<</N 406 0 R >>/DA(/ArialNarrow 10 Tf 0 g)/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/MK<<>>/P 138 0 R /Rect[ 64.313202 53.251202 578.34998 158.979996]/Subtype/Widget/T(Text18)/Type/Annot/V(I think I bring a calm, thoughtful voice to the conversation. I have experienced through my local board service and OSBA board service, budget crises, sudden leadership changes, and external pressure by people who don't always have a student focus. We have had challenging bargaining scenarios, and commuity concerns about safety in our schools. Having accurate information and sharing that information is crucial. One of my proudest moments was successfully leading OSBA in strongly supporting Measure 98. )>>
endobj
